  "title": "Counterweight Yard",
  "rules": [
    "Cargo cannot be carried upward on ladders; a crank operator raises it on a shared lift.",
    "Resting blocks and bracing workers on the opposite ballast pad support each loaded platform.",
    "Removing ballast can drop a loaded lift and stun its riders. Controlled lowering avoids that jolt.",
    "The shared brake stops both useful lift motion and automatic drops for its bounded duration.",
    "Bolt blocks into the three bridge sockets to create solid support; reclaiming a block opens a hole.",
    "Install one block at each side station and two in the middle. Material committed to private work is unavailable as ballast or bridge support."
  ],
